<section class="faq-section" style="background: var(--bg-cream);">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 900px;">
        <div class="faq-category">
            <h2>Appointments & Scheduling</h2>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>How do I schedule an appointment?</h3>
                <p>You can schedule an appointment by calling our office at <a href="tel:{{ site.phoneRaw }}">{{ site.phone }}</a> during business hours. We also offer a contact form on our website for appointment requests.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>How soon can I get an appointment?</h3>
                <p>We typically offer same-week appointments for most concerns. For urgent skin issues, please mention this when calling and we'll do our best to accommodate you as soon as possible.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What should I bring to my first appointment?</h3>
                <p>Please bring your insurance card, photo ID, a list of current medications, and any relevant medical records. If you have a specific skin concern, it helps to note when it started and any changes you've observed.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Do I need a referral to see a dermatologist?</h3>
                <p>Most insurance plans don't require a referral for dermatology visits, but some HMO plans do. We recommend checking with your insurance provider to confirm your specific requirements.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-category">
            <h2>Insurance & Payment</h2>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What insurance do you accept?</h3>
                <p>We accept most major insurance plans including Aetna, Blue Cross Blue Shield, Cigna, Humana, Medicare, SelectHealth, United Healthcare, and many more. Visit our <a href="{{ '/insurance/' | url }}">insurance page</a> for a complete list or call to verify your coverage.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What if I don't have insurance?</h3>
                <p>We offer competitive self-pay rates for patients without insurance. Please contact our office to discuss pricing and payment options, including payment plans for certain procedures.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Is cosmetic dermatology covered by insurance?</h3>
                <p>Most cosmetic procedures (Botox, cosmetic peels, etc.) are not covered by insurance. However, some treatments may be covered if they're medically necessary. We'll help you understand what's covered during your consultation.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-category">
            <h2>Services & Treatments</h2>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What conditions do you treat?</h3>
                <p>We treat all conditions affecting the skin, hair, and nails, including acne, eczema, psoriasis, rosacea, skin cancer, hair loss, nail disorders, rashes, warts, moles, and more. Visit our <a href="{{ '/conditions/' | url }}">conditions page</a> for more information.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Do you offer skin cancer screenings?</h3>
                <p>Yes! Skin cancer screenings are one of our most important services. We recommend annual full-body skin exams for most adults, especially those with risk factors like fair skin, history of sunburns, or family history of skin cancer.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>How long does a typical appointment last?</h3>
                <p>A standard dermatology visit typically lasts 15-30 minutes. Full-body skin exams may take a bit longer. Cosmetic consultations and procedures vary depending on the treatment.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Do you treat children?</h3>
                <p>Yes, we welcome patients of all ages. Our dermatologists have experience treating pediatric skin conditions including eczema, birthmarks, warts, and childhood acne.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-category">
            <h2>About Our Practice</h2>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Where are you located?</h3>
                <p>We're located at {{ site.address.full }}, near Thanksgiving Point. We serve patients throughout Utah County including American Fork, Saratoga Springs, Eagle Mountain, Pleasant Grove, and Draper.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>What are your office hours?</h3>
                <p>Monday, Tuesday, Thursday: 8:30 AM - 5:00 PM<br>Wednesday: 7:00 AM - 5:00 PM<br>Friday: 8:30 AM - 1:00 PM<br>Saturday & Sunday: Closed</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="faq-item">
                <h3>Is parking available?</h3>
                <p>Yes, we have a large free parking lot directly adjacent to our building with easy access to the main entrance.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
